"viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"ROCKET","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}},{"content":"EYES","viewerHasReacted":false,"reactors":{"totalCount":0,"nodes":[]}}],"__isNode":"IssueComment"},"cursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpPPAAABiig2m3AAqjE2OTE5MzkwOTI="},{"node":{"__typename":"IssueComment","databaseId":1692203985,"viewerDidAuthor":false,"issue":{"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"josepharhar","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2ODE0Njc="},"id":"I_kwDOCySmds5uu6Je","number":808,"locked":false,"databaseId":1857790558},"author":{"__typename":"User","login":"css-meeting-bot","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27466577?u=f1db811551a47160e3d78e2d4104d52f1fad7e13\u0026v=4","profileUrl":"https://github.com/css-meeting-bot","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDY2NTc3","name":"CSS Meeting Bot"},"id":"IC_kwDOCySmds5k3PvR","url":"https://github.com/openui/open-ui/issues/808#issuecomment-1692203985","createdAt":"2023-08-24T18:23:42Z","authorAssociation":"NONE","viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanMinimize":false,"viewerCanUnminimize":false,"viewerCanReport":false,"viewerCanReportToMaintainer":false,"viewerCanBlockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanUnblockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanBlockPersonally":false,"viewerCanUnblockPersonally":false,"viewerCanPin":false,"viewerCanUnpin":false,"viaApp":null,"minimizedReason":null,"showSpammyBadge":false,"createdViaEmail":false,"authorToRepoOwnerSponsorship":null,"viewerCanReadUserContentEdits":true,"lastEditedAt":null,"lastUserContentEdit":null,"pinnedBy":null,"body":"The Open UI Community Group just discussed `Naming of the selected value element`.\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\u003csummary\u003eThe full IRC log of that discussion\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u0026lt;masonf\u003e q?\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;masonf\u003e q+\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e jarhar: I proposed `\u0026lt;selectedvalue\u003e` as a replacement of behavior=selected-value\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e jarhar: but then we're rendering the selected option… so I would be in favour of calling this `\u0026lt;selectedoption\u003e`\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e masonf: I'm the only one on the queue… \u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e masonf: based on the offline conversations we had… this element is going to be pretty special\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e masonf: there probably would be future applications outside of this specific element… so maybe something like `\u0026lt;value\u003e` though I'm not very sure about that one\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;Luke\u003e q?\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;masonf\u003e ack masonf\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e masonf: I would like it if we could come up with a name that is applicable outside of `\u0026lt;selectlist\u003e`\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;Luke\u003e q+\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e Luke: it's more like the label of the option rather than the value… selectedoption could also be applied to other elements, like datalist\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e Luke: Maybe a more generic `\u0026lt;value\u003e` could be added in the future\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;masonf\u003e ack Luke\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;jarhar\u003e q+\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e jarhar: we could resolve to `\u0026lt;selectedoption\u003e` for now and keep the issue open?\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e masonf: to save yourself some time… would probably suggest to keep it open a bit longer or keep it the same\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e masonf: any objections to that proposed resolution?\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e scotto_: I'm trying to figure out where it could be use elsewhere where it wouldn't be an option that is chosen\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e scotto_: I'm all for reusability of stuff… \u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e masonf: maybe file input… and it receives the name of the file\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e scotto_: that doesn't make sense though… it's not an option, it's a file\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e masonf: my concern exactly\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e masonf: maybe `\u0026lt;currentselection\u003e` or something… `\u0026lt;currentcontent\u003e`\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e scotto_: this is outside the scope of this… I'm still trying to figure out how this is going to work and be returned\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e masonf: how the content of it is created?\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e scotto_: where does it go?\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e scotto_: is it something that can only go in that button[type=] that we talked about …is it always a child of the triggering element or is the expectation that it could be used somewhere else?\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e scotto_: if it always goes inside of the button… do we even need something there?\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e scotto_: I don't really understand\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e masonf: it does not have to be inside of the triggering button… it needs to be inside of the bounds of the rectangle that is the in page component that is the selectlist\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e masonf: otherwise only clicking on the down arrow causes the popup\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e masonf: it needs to be somewhere in the selectlist not necessarily the button\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e scotto_: I would wonder how that could get communicated to the accessibility tree\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;masonf\u003e q?\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;masonf\u003e ack jarhar\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e masonf: yes, a lot to be prototyped still\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e masonf: jarhar, do you want to resolve now to call it `\u0026lt;selectedoption\u003e` now?\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026lt;hdv\u003e jarhar: probably not if we end up needing to revert it soon anyway\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/details\u003e\n","bodyHTML":"\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThe Open UI Community Group just discussed \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003eNaming of the selected value element\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdetails\u003e\u003csummary\u003