f43db7a9d653fd4ad5a5f2\u0026v=4","profileUrl":"https://github.com/josepharhar","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2ODE0Njc=","name":"Joey Arhar"},"id":"IC_kwDOCySmds5lMaG1","url":"https://github.com/openui/open-ui/issues/808#issuecomment-1697751477","createdAt":"2023-08-29T16:09:27Z","authorAssociation":"COLLABORATOR","viewerCanDelete":false,"viewerCanMinimize":false,"viewerCanUnminimize":false,"viewerCanReport":false,"viewerCanReportToMaintainer":false,"viewerCanBlockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanUnblockFromOrg":false,"viewerCanBlockPersonally":false,"viewerCanUnblockPersonally":false,"viewerCanPin":false,"viewerCanUnpin":false,"viaApp":null,"minimizedReason":null,"showSpammyBadge":false,"createdViaEmail":false,"authorToRepoOwnerSponsorship":null,"viewerCanReadUserContentEdits":true,"lastEditedAt":null,"lastUserContentEdit":null,"pinnedBy":null,"body":"\u003e Why is this a tag, and not a property on the `\u003cselectlist\u003e` tag? It could simply be the `value` property, matching the pattern of other form elements.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure I understand what the API shape would look like.\r\nHere is an example of how selectedoption would be used:\r\n```html\r\n\u003cselectlist\u003e\r\n  \u003cbutton type=selectlist\u003e\r\n    \u003cspan\u003eselected option:\u003c/span\u003e\r\n    \u003cselectedoption\u003e\u003c/selectedoption\u003e\r\n  \u003c/button\u003e\r\n  \u003clistbox\u003e\r\n    \u003coption\u003eone\u003c/option\u003e\r\n    \u003coption\u003etwo\u003c/option\u003e\r\n  \u003c/listbox\u003e\r\n\u003c/selectlist\u003e\r\n```\r\nHow would you rewrite this without the selectedoption tag?","bodyHTML":"\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eWhy is this a tag, and not a property on the \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003e\u0026lt;selectlist\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e tag? It could simply be the \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003evalue\u003c/code\u003e property, matching the pattern of other form elements.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eI'm not sure I understand what the API shape would look like.\u003cbr\u003e\nHere is an example of how selectedoption would be used:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"highlight highlight-text-html-basic notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"\u0026lt;selectlist\u0026gt;\n  \u0026lt;button type=selectlist\u0026gt;\n    \u0026lt;span\u0026gt;selected option:\u0026lt;/span\u0026gt;\n    \u0026lt;selectedoption\u0026gt;\u0026lt;/selectedoption\u0026gt;\n  \u0026lt;/button\u0026gt;\n  \u0026lt;listbox\u0026gt;\n    \u0026lt;option\u0026gt;one\u0026lt;/option\u0026gt;\n    \u0026lt;option\u0026gt;two\u0026lt;/option\u0026gt;\n  \u0026lt;/listbox\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;/selectlist\u0026gt;\"\u003e\u003cpre class=\"notranslate\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e\u0026lt;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-ent\"\u003eselectlist\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n  \u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e\u0026lt;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-ent\"\u003ebutton\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003etype\u003c/span\u003e=\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003eselectlist\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e\u0026lt;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-ent\"\u003espan\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003eselected option:\u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e\u0026lt;/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-ent\"\u003espan\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e\u0026lt;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-ent\"\u003eselectedoption\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e\u0026lt;/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-ent\"\u003eselectedoption\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-kos\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e